{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgCpKBGzaWkvsHpvLF4yN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A visit delete from the patient chart is a soft delete (void), not a physical delete. The frontend sends a plain `DELETE`, which the REST layer turns into `VisitService.voidVisit`. That ends in `dao.saveVisit`, which is the actual database write. The hard-delete path (`purgeVisit` → `dao.deleteVisit`) is a separate route that the chart does not call.\n\n**Path for a delete from the chart (soft delete)**\n\n1. **Trigger:** `useDeleteVisit` calls `deleteVisit(activeVisit?.uuid)` (`openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-chart-app/src/visit/hooks/useDeleteVisit.tsx:59`).\n2. **Frontend request:** `deleteVisit(visitUuid)` sends `openmrsFetch(`${restBaseUrl}/visit/${visitUuid}`, { method: 'DELETE' })`. It sends no `purge` parameter (`openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-chart-app/src/visit/visits-widget/visit.resource.tsx:49-53`).\n3. **REST handler:** `VisitResource1_9.delete(visit, reason, context)` returns early if the visit is already voided, otherwise it calls `Context.getVisitService().voidVisit(visit, reason)` (`openmrs-module-webservices.rest/omod/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/webservices/rest/web/v1_0/resource/openmrs1_9/VisitResource1_9.java:270-277`).\n4. **Core service:** `VisitServiceImpl.voidVisit` returns `dao.saveVisit(visit)` (`openmrs-core/api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/api/impl/VisitServiceImpl.java:206-209`). The interface declaration is at `openmrs-core/api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/api/VisitService.java:255`.\n5. **Data access and DB write:** `VisitDAO.saveVisit` (`openmrs-core/api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/api/db/VisitDAO.java:86`) is implemented by `HibernateVisitDAO.saveVisit` (`openmrs-core/api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/api/db/hibernate/HibernateVisitDAO.java:167`). I did not read the body of `saveVisit`, so I have not confirmed the exact session call.\n\n**Hard-delete path (not used by the chart's delete button)**\n\n- `VisitResource1_9.purge` calls `Context.getVisitService().purgeVisit(visit)` (`openmrs-module-webservices.rest/.../openmrs1_9/VisitResource1_9.java:291-296`).\n- `VisitServiceImpl.purgeVisit` refuses if the visit has encounters (`APIException \"Visit.purge.inUse\"`), then calls `dao.deleteVisit(visit)` (`openmrs-core/api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/api/impl/VisitServiceImpl.java:222-231`). Declared in `VisitService.java:284`.\n- `HibernateVisitDAO.deleteVisit` calls `getCurrentSession().remove(visit)` (`openmrs-core/api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/api/db/hibernate/HibernateVisitDAO.java:174-178`). Declared in `VisitDAO.java:92`.\n\n**Not verified**\n\n- I did not confirm how webservices.rest routes a DELETE to `purge` instead of `delete` (for example via a `purge=true` query parameter in `DelegatingCrudResource`). The chart's request has no such parameter, so I am treating it as the soft-delete route.\n- I did not check whether `voided` is set by a core interceptor during `saveVisit`. `voidVisit` itself only saves the visit as given.\n- I did not check other callers of the REST `VisitResource` outside the chart.\n\n```json\n[\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-chart-app/src/visit/visits-widget/visit.resource.tsx\", \"startLine\": 49, \"endLine\": 53},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-esm-patient-chart/packages/esm-patient-chart-app/src/visit/hooks/useDeleteVisit.tsx\", \"startLine\": 59, \"endLine\": 59},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-module-webservices.rest/omod/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/webservices/rest/web/v1_0/resource/openmrs1_9/VisitResource1_9.java\", \"startLine\": 270, \"endLine\": 277},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-core/api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/api/impl/VisitServiceImpl.java\", \"startLine\": 206, \"endLine\": 209},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-core/api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/api/VisitService.java\", \"startLine\": 255, \"endLine\": 255},\n  {\"path\": \"openmrs-core/api/src/main/java/or